{"author":{"id":"2f242a7e7f2592f8909954a77fabece74f6e8cc197182647ed3b15ea8e3878af"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791024466,"nonce":"eu57mlWnf1Zxt2zw6QzUbN8IWLI=","title":"a page cannot read the clipboard","message":"Window.clipboardText answers none in a page: navigator.clipboard.readText is asynchronous and asks the user's permission, so web.rs has nothing to return synchronously. setClipboardText works there, through the agent's writeClipboard, gated on the user's activation.\n\nA page normally receives pasted text as a `paste` ClipboardEvent on the focused element, with the text in clipboardData, in answer to the user's own paste. The agent could post that as an event, for instance a new Event variant carrying the text, which a text field takes the way it takes Ime commits. That changes the Event declaration and the agent's XwEvent, so it waits until a program in a page needs paste (ashui's text field will, once it runs in a page).","files":null}]}